  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capital Contribution for the facilitation of High Risk&#x2013;High Impact Investments in Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this contribution is to enhance IFU&#x2019;s investments lower income African countries. The country focus will be complemented with a high-impact focus in order to priorities investments, which are expected to generate high development outcomes closely related to the SDGs in local economies, but where the expected risk adjusted return would be lower than what IFU can normally accept. This additional contribution under the 2021 Finance Act shall be used for climate investments. In addition to that the HRHI contribution will contribute to the generation of decent jobs  and in particular women and youth, bottom-of the pyramid, smallholder agriculture, access to affordable and clean energy, and MSME. The blended concessional finance initiative will be integrated into IFU&#x2019;s governance structure, and be managed according to current policies and strategies.

Development objective: Enhanced IFU contribution to job climate investments, job creation and inclusive green growth in lower income countries in Africa.
Immediate objectives:
1. Blended concessional finance initiative developed and in operation with increased volume of IFU investments in climate projects with high development outcomes in the lower income countries in Africa.
2. Promote and accelerate IFU&#x2019;s development of procedures for and experience with identifying and managing projects with high development outcomes in lower income countries in Africa.</narrative>
  </description>
